    "result": "`parse_line` is implemented in `solution.py` and the test suite in `tests/test_solution.py` passes: `python -m pytest -q tests` reports 33 passed. I could not run a coverage tool, since the only shell command allowed was the test command. By reading the code, every line of `solution.py` is exercised: the type and separator checks, both quoted-field paths (doubled quotes, unclosed quote, junk after the closing quote), the unquoted-field path with its `\"`/`\\r`/`\\n` rejection, and the separator-skip and end-of-line returns. The signature `parse_line(line: str, sep: str = \",\") -> list[str]` is unchanged. Validation runs type checks first, then separator checks, then parsing. The tests cover the spec's examples, whitespace preservation, custom separators, and every `ValueError` and `TypeError` case in the spec. No other files were created or modified.",
